    "created_at": "2018-09-29T17:11:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-09-29T17:11:48Z",
    "body": "If I were to add it to serialport, I'd handle it underneath our node streams layer at the [binding layer](https://serialport.io/docs/api-bindings) and which would probably expose it as a configuration settings, for choosing the error character and if possible having it produce a read error. I need to do [more research](https://github.com/node-serialport/node-serialport/issues/1684) to know what's possible.\r\n\r\nOur bindings needs better docs but it looks something like [this](https://serialport.io/docs/api-binding-abstract) and I'm working on a next version with lessons learned on this spec https://github.com/node-serialport/node-serialport/issues/1679 I'm still exploring the api. Since the binding layer is closer to the actual syscalls and doesn't have a concept of a stream, we can use it to build node streams, `ReadableStream`, async iterator, or whatever interface is de jour.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
